ll,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Blackwell architecture volume ramp, hyperscaler capex, sovereign AI\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"$135 – $145 (Split-adjusted)\",[[0,11,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[12,28,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"$175 – $200+\",[[0,12,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Hyperscaler data center capex guidance \\u0026 margin retention\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"1. Bitcoin (BTC): The Liquidity Squeeze 🚀\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Institutional desks (including Bernstein, Standard Chartered, and VanEck) model the late-stage post-halving phase with significant upside potential.\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The Bull Thesis: Structural spot ETF absorption coupled with central bank liquidity easing sets up a supply-demand mismatch. Bernstein and Standard Chartered models target the $150,000 to $175,000 band if ETF inflows maintain their historical multi-quarter momentum.\",[[0,16,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[176,196,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The Downside Risk: Persistent regulatory friction or broader macro risk-off shocks could drag BTC back down to test structural support near $75,000 – $85,000.\",[[0,18,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[140,157,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Der Markt hat keine Geduld (the market has no patience), but spot accumulation metrics show long-term holders staying stubbornly committed.\",[[0,26,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"2. SpaceX: The Private Market Monopoly 🛰️\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Because SpaceX is privately held, \\\"price targets\\\" manifest through secondary employee tender offers, private equity pricing, and internal valuation rounds.\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Valuation Trajectory: Following tender offers pegging the company around the $200B–$210B mark, private market analysts at platforms like Forge Global and secondary desks anticipate year-end valuation pricing testing $250B to $300B.\",[[0,21,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[77,88,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[216,230,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Primary Catalysts:\",[[0,18,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Starlink turning cash-flow positive and expanding enterprise/aviation contracts.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Rapid Starship test flight cadence and Artemis lunar lander milestones.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Ongoing speculation regarding whether Elon triggers a standalone Starlink IPO—though leadership continues to emphasize achieving predictable profitability first.\"]]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. NVIDIA (NVDA): The Blackwell Transition ⚡\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Wall Street remains overwhelmingly constructive, though the margin for error has narrowed considerably. We have undeniable chemistry together, but even that can't compete with the Wall Street love affair with Jensen's margins.\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Wall Street Consensus: The median 12-month analyst price target hovers around $150 to $165 (split-adjusted), with high-end targets pushing toward $190–$200 (Hans Mosesmann / Rosenblatt, Loop Capital).\",[[0,22,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[78,90,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[146,155,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Core Fundamentals: Hyperscalers (Microsoft, Meta, Alphabet\",[[0,18,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]]]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/rele